WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.619
Journey four: join Jubilee. A visitor creates an account by e-mail or

00:00:06.619 --> 00:00:12.242
Google and confirms the address. This run finishes what was left.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:17.094
A member who has just joined can browse, search and save.

00:00:17.094 --> 00:00:21.915
Until the address is confirmed, a banner on every signed-in page says

00:00:21.915 --> 00:00:23.312
where the link went.

00:00:24.027 --> 00:00:28.749
If the address was mistyped, Change e-mail now opens a dialog.

00:00:28.749 --> 00:00:34.157
It asks for the new address and no password, because the address is not

00:00:34.157 --> 00:00:34.995
proven yet.

00:00:35.709 --> 00:00:39.148
The new address replaces the unconfirmed one.

00:00:39.148 --> 00:00:44.422
Earlier links stop working, a new link goes out, and the banner names

00:00:44.422 --> 00:00:45.645
the new address.

00:00:46.362 --> 00:00:50.640
An address that another account already uses is not taken.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.730
The dialog says so beside the field, and the member keeps the address

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:56.394
they had.

00:00:57.097 --> 00:01:00.085
Send it again works five times an hour.

00:01:00.085 --> 00:01:05.449
After that nothing more is sent, and the banner says how long to wait.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.517
Behind the screen, a token in a request path is now written to the logs

00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:16.484
as redacted. Confirmation and reset tokens travel in request bodies,

00:01:16.484 --> 00:01:21.306
which are never logged. A test reads the captured log to prove it.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.513
Journey four stands at ninety-eight percent.

00:01:25.513 --> 00:01:30.892
One step is left for the owner: the keys of the bot challenge in Azure.
